  heroHeadline: "Connect Your CRM to the Rest of the Business, Without Duplicates or Dead Leads",
  heroTagline: "We integrate HubSpot, Salesforce, GoHighLevel and Zoho CRM with your accounting, job management, forms, telephony, ad platforms and custom software, so leads route correctly, records stay clean and nobody retypes a customer twice.",
  summaryStatement: "CRM integration is the work of connecting a customer relationship management platform, such as HubSpot, Salesforce, GoHighLevel or Zoho CRM, to the other systems a business runs, through their APIs and webhooks, so contacts, deals, activities and invoices stay consistent across them and automations act on accurate data.",
  description: [
    "A CRM is only as useful as the data in it. Most of the CRM problems we are asked about are not CRM problems at all: leads from the website form arrive without the campaign that produced them, the same customer exists three times with different spellings, a won deal still has to be typed into Xero or MYOB by hand, the job system and the CRM disagree about whether a customer is active, and the sales team stops trusting the reports. Integration fixes the plumbing so the CRM reflects what is really happening in the business.",
    "Typical integrations for Australian businesses connect the CRM to accounting (a won deal or signed quote becomes an invoice, and payment status flows back), to job or project management such as ServiceM8 or simPRO, to web forms, booking tools and live chat, to telephony and SMS so calls and messages are logged against the contact, to ad platforms so offline conversions are reported back, and to a company's own app or customer portal. Each one is a decision about which system owns which field, what happens when they disagree, and who is told when something fails.",
    "Each platform sets limits that shape the design, and they change, so treat these as at the time of writing (November 2026). HubSpot's usage guidelines give privately distributed apps a burst limit of 100 requests per 10 seconds on Free and Starter and 190 on Professional and Enterprise, with daily limits of 250,000, 625,000 and 1,000,000 requests per account respectively. GoHighLevel's API documentation lists a burst limit of 100 requests per 10 seconds and 200,000 requests per day, counted per app per sub account or company. Zoho CRM uses API credits in a 24 hour window that scale with edition and user licences, from 5,000 on the Free edition upward. Salesforce allocates API requests by edition and licence count, visible in your org's setup. A good integration batches, uses webhooks instead of polling, and queues work so a busy campaign does not hit a limit and drop leads.",
    "We use GoHighLevel in our own business, so we know its strengths and its quirks first hand, and we will tell you when a native feature or an existing marketplace app does the job better than custom code. We hold no HubSpot, Salesforce, GoHighLevel or Zoho partner tier; we build against each vendor's published APIs. Senior engineers lead every build and review every change, and you receive updates every Tuesday and Friday, Sydney time.",
